      "summaryMarkdown": "All five criteria are met. F-s2-1 is resolved by ff08766: release-plz.toml sets release_commits = \"^(feat|fix|perf)\", tests/release_automation.rs asserts it, and docs/releasing.md now states which commit types release and that breaking changes must be written feat!/fix!/perf!. A scratch run of release-plz 0.3.172 against ff08766 confirmed docs, chore(agentx) and refactor! commits produce no release, perf gives 1.0.1 and feat gives 1.1.0. Earlier checks stand: no-tag initial release is a no-op for release-pr, the changelog inserts above the hand-written 1.0.0 section, the 9 release_automation tests pass. GitHub cannot list release-plz.yml before it is on main (observed in s5, t08), and RELEASE_PLZ_TOKEN must exist before the first push to main that contains the workflow.",
      "findingIds": [
