      "descriptionMarkdown": "Expected: docs/releasing.md says `docs:`, `test:`, `ci:`, `chore:`, `refactor:` commits cause 'no release on their own', and release PRs only follow releasable commits. Observed (release-plz 0.3.172, scratch clone of HEAD with tag v1.0.0, `release-plz update --config release-plz.toml`): any commit that touches the package (the package is the whole repository) bumps the patch version: `docs:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `ci:`, `test:` and even a `chore(agentx)` commit that only changes `.agentx/memory/a.md` each produce `1.0.0 -> 1.0.1`. So the doc table is wrong, and every `chore(agentx)` sprint sync on main would open or refresh a release PR with an empty or noise-only changelog. Repair: add `release_commits = \"^(feat|fix|perf)\"` to `[workspace]` in release-plz.toml (verified in the scratch clone: docs/chore/chore(agentx) commits then produce no update, `fix` -> 1.0.1, `perf` -> 1.0.1, `feat!` -> 2.0.0, and docs commits are still listed in the changelog when a `fix` triggers the release). Assert the key in tests/release_automation.rs (changelog/config test). Then make docs/releasing.md match: state that only `feat`, `fix` and `perf` commits (and their `!` forms) start a release, that other types are listed in the next one, and that a breaking change must be marked on a `feat!`/`fix!`/`perf!` commit (a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer on another type does not trigger a release); or widen the regex to `^(feat|fix|perf)|!:` and say so. If the owner prefers every commit to release, instead correct the table to say so and drop the 'no release on their own' row.",
