      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** DEP-1 accepts crates.io only (plus pinned public git); a dependency a clean clone cannot fetch must be rejected. **Observed:** a dependency from an alternative (private/other) registry passes both gates. `dependency_violations` never looks at the `registry` / `registry-index` keys, and `source_violation` returns `None` for any source starting with `registry+` (`tests/dependency_sources.rs`, `source_violation`), so `foo = { version = \"1\", registry = \"internal\" }` and a Cargo.lock/`cargo metadata` source `registry+https://private.example/index` are accepted. (Verified by reading the code paths; the previous `package_layout` test had the same `starts_with(\"registry+\")` looseness, but DEP-1 and the DEP-2 rule text say crates.io.)\n\n**Repair:** (1) in `dependency_violations` push a violation when `spec` contains `registry` or `registry-index` (the same for `[patch]` entries, which go through it); (2) in `source_violation` accept only exactly `registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index` (what cargo prints for crates.io, including with the sparse protocol; the real lockfile already uses it) and reject any other `registry+`/`sparse+` source; (3) add inline reject cases: `registry = \"internal\"`, `registry-index = \"https://example.com/index\"` in `[dependencies]` and in a `[patch.crates-io]` entry, and a `source_violation(\"a\", \"registry+https://private.example/index\")` assertion.",
